Source: deb-find-changes
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Gavin Carr <gavin@profound.net>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: deb-find-changes
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: cron | cron-daemon
Description: List orphaned and locally-modified files for backup on Debian
 deb-find-changes walks one or more directory trees (default /etc) and
 lists the files that are not owned by any installed dpkg package
 (orphans) or that differ from their packaged checksums (modified). It
 reads the dpkg database directly, so it is fast and needs no per-file
 dpkg calls.
 .
 The list is intended for the extract backup tool. A nightly cron job
 writes it to /var/cache/deb-find-changes/etc.txt, and an initial scan is
 run when the package is first installed.
 .
 Distributed as a pure-Go statically-linked executable (CGO disabled).
